MEM SIZE? REM t30: CMD -- the Model III TRSDOS 1.3 CMD"&"& easter egg, and the forms

R/S L2 BASIC
------------------------------
TRS-80 LEVEL II BASIC emulator
 Codeveloped with Claude, 2026
------------------------------
man pages available for all BASIC commands
"help meta" to display supported metacommands
READY
>REM around it that must keep behaving exactly as they did before it existed
READY
>10 ON ERROR GOTO 500
>20 CMD"&"&
>30 PRINT "A":CMD"&"&:PRINT "B"
>40 CMD=5: PRINT "CMD AS VARIABLE";CMD
>50 T=1: CMD"&"
>60 T=2: CMD"S"
>70 T=3: A$="&": CMD A$
>80 T=4: CMD"&"&X
>90 PRINT "TRAPPED";N: END
>500 N=N+1: PRINT "SN AT";T;(ERR=2): RESUME NEXT
>RUN
